{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0134VTcC14czeQHZkAhfupVF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified by differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a specification-driven code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: SRDs (specs) → mage-claude-orchestrator (synthesis) → differential testing (verification). Shared libraries in pkg/ (sys, format, testutils, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), per-utility packages in cmd/.\n\n**Current state**: Most releases have partial implementation. Recent work completed srd108-vdir R1.1-R2.2 (tasks 5612, 5613).\n\n**Current release**: Release 13.0 is the earliest release with \"ready\" requirements — srd106-df (R3.1-R4.3), srd108-vdir (R2.3-R2.4), and srd109-dircolors (R1.1-R3.5).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 13.0 has three utilities with ready requirements. I prioritize:\n1. **df** (cmd/df) — 10 ready requirements (R3.1-R4.3), package exists (R1-R2 completed)\n2. **vdir** (cmd/vdir) — 2 ready requirements (R2.3-R2.4), nearly complete\n3. **dircolors** (cmd/dircolors) — 15 ready requirements, brand new package\n\nWith the 4-task limit, I propose 3 df tasks + 1 vdir task, completing vdir and all remaining df requirements. Dircolors deferred to next batch.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n```\nTask 0: srd106-df R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R3.3 (w=1), R3.4 (w=1) → total = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd106-df R3.5 (w=1), R3.6 (w=1), R3.7 (w=1) → total = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd106-df R4.1 (w=1), R4.2 (w=1), R4.3 (w=1) → total = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd108-vdir R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1) → total = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n(Weights assumed 1; requirements.yaml not available inline. Orchestrator validates actual weights.)\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/df: implement srd106 R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd106-df.yaml (SRD with requirement definitions for R3.1-R3.4)\n      - cmd/df/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.x and R2.x)\n      - cmd/df/df_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/format/format.go (HumanSize and formatting helpers used by df)\n      - pkg/sys/stat.go (filesystem metadata abstractions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/df/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add implementation for srd106-df requirements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4\n      - path: cmd/df/df_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases covering R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd106-df requirement R3.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd106-df requirement R3.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd106-df requirement R3.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd106-df requirement R3.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing cmd/df implementation -- do not rewrite code that already satisfies R1.x and R2.x requirements\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Add differential tests using testutils.RunDiffTests comparing against the gdf reference binary from Homebrew coreutils\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment to ensure output parity between Go and GNU binaries\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/df ./cmd/df/ succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/df/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/df/ -count=1 passes (skips gracefully if gdf not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Each of R3.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4 has at least one differential test case in df_test.go\"\n\n- index: 1\n  